        "predicate": "vector_addition_diagram",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Adding Vectors: Tip-to-Tail Method",
          "description": "Two or more vectors can be combined to find a resultant vector using the tip-to-tail method. Draw the first vector from a starting point, then draw the second vector starting from the tip of the first. The resultant is drawn from the original starting point to the final tip. This graphical method beautifully shows how vectors combine. When analyzing projectile motion, we often reverse this process: we decompose the initial velocity vector (a single vector with magnitude and direction) into horizontal and vertical components, which we then analyze separately. Look at the diagram on the Vector Board to see the tip-to-tail addition of two velocity vectors."
        },
