        "location": "launch_zone",
        "predicate": "angle_measurement_label",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Launch Your First Projectile",
          "description": "Now let's apply vector concepts to real projectile motion. You are ready to launch a projectile at a 45-degree angle with an initial speed of 20 m/s. The launcher's angle can be adjusted using the angle control dial. At 45 degrees, the initial velocity vector is decomposed into equal horizontal and vertical components: Vx \u2248 14.1 m/s and Vy \u2248 14.1 m/s. Watch what happens when you fire the launcher. Observe the parabolic path\u2014this is the combined result of (1) constant horizontal motion (Vx remains 14.1 m/s throughout) and (2) vertical motion under gravity (Vy decreases to zero at the peak, then becomes negative as the projectile falls)."
        },
